 "id": "zenodo:18692967",
 "title": "Raman microscopy of live Saccharomyces cerevisiae yeast",
 "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/18692967",
 "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.18692967",
 "description": "<p>We acquired coherent Raman microscopy data on budding yeast<em> Saccharomyces cerevisiae</em> (wild-type) and two mutants, aah1∆ and rad6∆. Our aim was to collect spatially resolved biochemical data on living yeast cells. The image preview (rgb_overlay_BY4741_WT.png) is a composite of three single-wavenumber SRS acquisitions, taken at 1,650 (red), 2,850 (green) and 2,937 cm&minus;1 (blue).&nbsp;</p>\n<p>This record contains the raw LIF files and metadata in JSON and CSV format. This release accompanies the pub&nbsp;<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.57844/arcadia-mxf9-th4q\">\"Coherent Raman imaging of live, unfixed Saccharomyces cerevisiae and mutants aah1∆ and rad6∆\"</a>, and the GitHub repository for visualizing the dataset and exporting images and metadata is&nbsp;<a href=\"https://github.com/Arcadia-Science/2026-scerevisiae-dataset\">here</a>.&nbsp;</p>",
 "found_by_keywords": [
  "science"
 ],
